================================================================================
Third-party models
================================================================================

HearWrite's base install (`pip install hearwrite`) contains no third-party model
code and downloads no weights. Everything below arrives only with an optional
extra, and each carries its own terms that you inherit when you use it.

This file is the licensing map. It is maintained deliberately, because "which
licence did that checkpoint have" is exactly the question nobody wants to answer
after shipping.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
hearwrite[onnx] -- the default backend. Permissive, ungated, CPU-only.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  sherpa-onnx (k2-fsa)                     Apache-2.0
    Streaming transducer runtime and the speaker segmentation / embedding
    models. https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx

  Silero VAD (snakers4/silero-vad)         MIT
    https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
    NOTE: distinct from `silero-models` (the STT/TTS repo), which is
    CC-BY-NC-SA. Only the VAD is used here, and it has been MIT throughout.

  nemotron-3.5-asr-streaming-0.6b (NVIDIA) OpenMDW-1.1
    Optional multilingual streaming checkpoint. Permissive; requires notices to
    be preserved. https://huggingface.co/nvidia/nemotron-3.5-asr-streaming-0.6b

  NeMo TitaNet small (NVIDIA)              CC-BY-4.0   <- attribution required
    Speaker embeddings, 192 dimensions. Redistributed ungated by sherpa-onnx.
    The default speaker frontend.
    https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/tag/speaker-recongition-models

  WeSpeaker CAM++ (wenet-e2e)              Apache-2.0
    Alternative speaker embeddings. Not the default: measured separation on
    real speakers is poor. See docs/evaluation.md.

  smart-turn v3 (pipecat-ai)               BSD-2-Clause  [code AND weights]
    Semantic turn detection. Vendored under src/hearwrite/vendor/, with its
    LICENSE alongside. https://github.com/pipecat-ai/smart-turn

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
hearwrite[whisper] -- second engine
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  faster-whisper (SYSTRAN)                 MIT
  CTranslate2 (OpenNMT)                    MIT
  Whisper checkpoints (OpenAI)             MIT / Apache-2.0

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
hearwrite[sortformer] -- optional diarization backend (needs torch)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  diar_streaming_sortformer_4spk-v2        CC-BY-4.0   <- attribution required
    Handles at most 4 speakers. NVIDIA.
    https://huggingface.co/nvidia/diar_streaming_sortformer_4spk-v2
    We pin v2 (CC-BY-4.0) rather than v2.1, which is under the NVIDIA Open
    Model Licence -- commercially usable, but not OSI-approved and carrying a
    patent-litigation termination clause.

  NeMo (NVIDIA-NeMo/Speech)                Apache-2.0

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Deliberately NOT used
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  pyannote community-1 / 3.1   CC-BY-4.0 and MIT respectively, but gated behind
                               a Hugging Face acceptance. Gating means a token
                               in CI and weights that cannot be vendored, which
                               breaks the "clone and run" property.
  LiveKit turn-detector        Weights are under the proprietary LiveKit Model
                               Licence, and the plugin package is deprecated.
                               smart-turn is used instead.
